 The security model should be measurable and formally specified before being trusted.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 14 — Full-system integration, validation, and stability
+
+Status: **implemented in the Phase 14 validation branch**
+
+This is a post-roadmap integration phase. Its purpose is to prove that the existing
+AI-native primitives behave coherently before adding another large subsystem.
+
+Implemented validation surfaces:
+
+- work-graph structural validation
+- missing/self/duplicate dependency detection
+- DAG cycle detection
+- scheduler deadlock detection
+- deterministic scheduler accounting (picks, dispatches, candidate scans)
+- tensor size/location accounting
+- allocation accounting and high-water tracking
+- capability isolation checks
+- repeated end-to-end graph stress execution
+- host-side regression suite using the same core C sources as the kernel
+- freestanding kernel self-test gate during boot
+
+Current deterministic benchmark scenarios use 4, 8, 16, and 32-node chains. They
+measure scheduler work in candidate scans rather than wall-clock latency because the
+original starter substrate does not yet expose a calibrated monotonic clock to this
+branch.
+
+Exit criteria for this implementation:
+
+- all Phase 14 host regression tests pass
+- sanitizer pass is clean
+- freestanding kernel compiles and links with warnings treated as errors
+- malformed/cyclic graphs are rejected
+- scheduler deadlock is surfaced rather than silently stalling
+- 48 repeated end-to-end stress rounds complete
+- memory accounting remains within the early-heap capacity
+
+A later hardware/runtime phase should add calibrated latency, throughput, tail-latency,
+DMA, accelerator, and real workload benchmarks once those facilities are available.
